      "displayPolicyNote": "1913-09-07 selected Serbian Приштина; 1974-02-27 selected Albanian Prishtina / Serbian Приштина as concurrent official native forms (Turkish public-language rights do not require Turkish map-name co-display); 1990-09-28 selected Serbian Приштина alone as an editorial threshold anchored to Serbia's constitution and subsequent restrictive administration; 2000-07-27 selected Albanian/Serbian forms together again based on UNMIK Regulation 2000/43, reinforced by UNMIK Regulation 2000/45 of 2000-08-11 requiring both languages on official signage. The 1990 Constitution's Article 8 still contemplated minority official-language use under statute, so 1990 is not an asserted total Albanian-language ban or a city rename. Albanian Prishtina remained in community use; real-world 2000 bilingual signage implementation was uneven. Korean 프리슈티나 and English Pristina remain unchanged."
